WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
Some atoms have unstable nuclei.

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.100
Each one decays and gives out radiation.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.240
But which nucleus goes next?

4
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.260
Nobody can predict it.

5
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.960
Decay is random.

6
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:17.100
Heat it, squeeze it, bond it to other
atoms: the rate barely changes.

7
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.280
Yet decay is used to date ancient bones.

8
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.540
So how can atoms that decay at
random tell us how old a bone is?

9
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.400
In this mission, you'll balance
nuclear equations for alpha,

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.540
beta and gamma decay, and test each one
against paper, metal and electric fields.

11
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.980
Then you'll find the order
hidden inside random decay,

12
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.380
and see radioisotopes at work
in medicine and industry.

13
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.600
Your mission: find out how random
decay can tell the age of a bone.